<LegalPageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Landscape Estimate Pro"
  description="How Landscape Estimate Pro handles your data. No customer, project, estimate, quote, or financial data leaves your device."
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  updated="January 2026"
>
  <h2>Local-first by design</h2>
  <p>
    Landscape Estimate Pro's calculators, templates, and Pro application run entirely in your browser. No customer,
    project, estimate, quote, or financial data leaves your device. The materials, labor rates, equipment,
    assemblies, projects, and estimates you enter are stored in your browser's local storage, on your own device.
    We do not operate a database that stores your business or project data.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do collect</h2>
  <p>
    The public website (the marketing pages you're reading right now, and the free calculators) may use
    privacy-conscious anonymous traffic analytics when enabled — aggregate page-view counts, not individual
    tracking. This analytics is never active inside the Pro application workspace itself, and it never receives
    customer names, addresses, project names, service descriptions, estimate or quote values, project or quote IDs,
    imported filenames, or anything else you've entered into your workspace. Purchasing isn't open yet, so no
    payment information is collected at all — see our <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a> for the current state.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The public website may use an analytics cookie to understand aggregate traffic. No advertising cookies are used
    to build a profile of you across other sites, and there is no account or login cookie of any kind — the Pro
    application has no login and sets no cookie at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data, your control</h2>
  <p>
    Because your workspace lives in your browser, clearing your browser's site data for this domain will remove it.
    Pro includes a JSON export/import feature specifically so you can back up your workspace or move it to a new
    device or browser before that happens.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to the contact information provided elsewhere on this site.</p>
</LegalPageLayout>
